<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000777> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heat capacity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000777> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die Wärmekapazität ist eine thermische Eigenschaft, die die Menge an Wärmeenergie beschreibt, die erforderlich ist, um die Temperatur einer Entität um einen bestimmten Betrag zu erhöhen."@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000777> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The heat capacity is a thermal property describing the amount of heat energy required to raise the temperature of an entity by a given amount."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000777> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000778
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000778> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000778> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000833> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000778> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "Mixing two fluids. Adding salt into water."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000778> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mixing"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000778> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material processing with the objective to combine two or more material entities as input into a single material entity as output."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000779
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000779> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000779> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000550> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000779> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "Official definition can be found in: DIN EN ISO 4885:2018 Wärmebehandlung Page 21, 3.108 Wärmebehandlung - Definition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000779> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "Offizielle Definition findet man in: DIN EN ISO 4885:2018 Wärmebehandlung Seite 21, 3.108 Wärmebehandlung - Definition"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000779> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Wärmebehandlung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000779> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heat treatment"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000779> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Wärmebehandeln"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000779> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A changing properties of material process in which a solid (ferrous) product is fully or partially exposed to specific time-temperature sequences through a series of process steps with the aim of modifying its properties and/or its internal structure."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000779> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ein Stoffeigenschaft Ändern Prozess, bei dem durch eine Reihe von Verfahrensschritten ein festes (Eisen-)Produkt ganz oder teilweise bestimmten Zeit-Temperatur-Abfolgen ausgesetzt wird, mit dem Ziel, seine Eigenschaften und/oder seine innere Struktur zu modifizieren."@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000779> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Annealing, Ageing, Hardening"@en .
