# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000851
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000851> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000851> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020164> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000851> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000851> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Joerg Waitelonis" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000851> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Schmelzpunkt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000851> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "melting point"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000851> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Der Schmelzpunkt ist eine Zustandsgrenze einer Materie, die durch den Übergang vom festen in den flüssigen Zustand (oder umgekehrt) entsteht."@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000851> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The melting point is a state of matter boundary realized by transition form the solid state to the liquid state (or vice versa)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000851> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
