<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0010034> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "curing"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0010034> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#comment> "Curing may be induced by thermal energy, radiation, atmospheric exposure, or chemical additives. It applies broadly to material systems including polymer resins, concrete, vulcanized rubbers, drying oils, and coatings." .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0010034> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A curing process is a material processing process in which a material entity undergoes physical or chemical transformation to reach a hardened, set, or macroscopically stabilized state."@en .
