<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020130> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "thermodynamic driving force"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020130> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The driving force for a phase transformation or mass transfer is proportional to the difference in chemical potential between phases\n\nΔμ=μα−μβ, with chemical potential μ and phases α and β" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020130> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "For α → β: ΔG = G_β − G_α. If ΔG < 0, the transformation is thermodynamically favorable; many report the driving force as F = −ΔG > 0" .
