# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020190
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020190> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020190> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000965> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020190> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020190> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Philipp von Hartrott" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020190> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "metallografischer Schnitt (Oberfläche)"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020190> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "metallographic section (surface)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020190> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A surface layer (fiat object part) of an object which at the same time is a metal and the object is specified output of a planned process which describes the preparation of the surface."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020190> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Eine Oberflächenschicht (Fiat-Objektteil) eines Objekts, die gleichzeitig ein Metall ist und das Objekt ist das spezifizierte Ergebnis eines geplanten Prozesses, der die Vorbereitung der Oberfläche beschreibt."@de .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020191
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020191> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020191> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000030> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020191> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Typical dimensions of the round mountings are a diameter of 20-50 mm and a thickness of 10-20 mm."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020191> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "metallographic section (embedded sample)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A metallographic section (embedded sample) is an object that has two parts: a metallic object that has a metallographic section (surface) as part and the mounting which is produced during a hot embedding or cold embedding process."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020192
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020192> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020192> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020190> .
