<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "material reacting process has always energy minimization as a driving force."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "material reacting process"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "materieller Reaktionsprozess"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025009> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ein materieller Reaktionsprozess ist ein Prozess, der in einem Teil der Materie aufgrund einiger seiner Dispositionen oder Verhaltenseigenschaften stattfindet, die in einem stimulierenden Prozess umgesetzt werden. Sowohl der materielle Reaktionsprozess als auch der stimulierende Prozess müssen stattfindende Teile eines geplanten Prozesses sein, wenn der geplante Prozess stattfindet."@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025009> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Material reacting process is a process which occurs in a portion of matter due to some of its disposition or behavioral material property which has realization in some  stimulating process. Both the material reacting process and stimulating process must be occurent parts of a planned process, if the planned process takes place."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025010
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025010> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000549> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025010> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
