<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "amorphous material"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025030> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#comment> "old axiom (material and ('has quality' some ('order scale' and 'specified by value' value 'short range order')))" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025030> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An amorphous material is a material that has a short-range atomic order"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025030> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Glass" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025030> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0001032> "https://github.com/materialdigital/core-ontology/issues/458" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025031
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025031> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025025> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "short-range order"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025031> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "short-range order is a range order characterized by structural organization of members of an object aggregate strictly confined to the nearest neighbours and immediate chemical bonds"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025031> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Ordering of atoms in amorphous materials"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025032
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025032> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025032> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025025> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025032> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "long-range order"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025032> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "long-range order is a range order characterized by repeating periodicity across macroscopic distances in an object aggregate"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025032> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "ordering of atoms in a crystalline material"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025033
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025033> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025025> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "medium-range order"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025033> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "medium-range order is a range order that characterizes structural organization of members of an object aggregate where small atomic groups link into localized patterns that do not repeat across the whole material"@en .
