# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020132> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'length' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'DimensionQuality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000122."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Lars Vogt" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Length is a size that describes the spatial extent of its bearer in one dimension."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Länge"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "length"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "dimension"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die Länge ist eine eindimensionale Größe."@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Length is a one dimensional size."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A steel rod measures 250 mm in length between its two end faces"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
