<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050154> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Breite"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050154> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "width"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050154> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/2.0.8/Width> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050154> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/width> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050154> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Diese Klasse beschreibt eine horizontale Messung eines Objekts, die im rechten Winkel zur Länge des Objekts vorgenommen wird."@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050154> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "This class describes a horizontal measurement of an object taken at right angles to the length of the object."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050155
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050155> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050155> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050155> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050155> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Markus Schilling" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050155> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "“Shape.” Merriam-Webster.com Dictionary, Merriam-Webster, https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/shape. Accessed 13 Jan. 2023." .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050155> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Form"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050155> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "shape"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050155> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Das sichtbare Ausstattungsmerkmal (räumliche Form oder Kontur) eines bestimmten Objektes oder einer Art von Objekt."@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050155> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Extemsive quality, the visible makeup characteristic (spatial form or contour) of a particular item or kind of item."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050156
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050156> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050156> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050155> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050156> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050156> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Markus Schilling" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050156> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "DIN EN ISO 6892-1:2019" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050156> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Geometrische Form"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050156> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "geometry shape"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050156> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Dieses Konzept beschreibt die geometrischen Abmessungen und das Erscheinungsbild (Form und Abmaße) einer Probe, eines Prüfkörpers oder eines Prüfstücks, wie sie üblicherweise durch eine entsprechende Norm definiert sind. Dementsprechend ist der angegebene Formwert in Übereinstimmung mit der definierenden Norm anzugeben, z. B. \"Zugprüfstück Form 1 gemäß Anhang B der Zugversuchsnorm\"."@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050156> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "This concept describes the geometric dimensions and appearance (shape and dimensions) of a sample, specimen, or test piece as usually defined by a corresponding standard. Accordingly, the shape value given is in accordance with the defining standard, e.g., ‘tensile test piece shape 1 in accordance with annex B of the tensile test standard’."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050157
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050157> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050157> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050156> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050157> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050157> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Markus Schilling" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050157> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "3D Geometrie"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050157> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "shape 3d"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050157> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A shape 3D is a geometry shape that exists in three dimensions, having length, width, and height, and can be defined by its spatial properties such as volume and surface area."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050157> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Eine 3D Geometrie ist eine geometrische Form, die in drei Dimensionen existiert, mit Länge, Breite und Höhe, und die durch ihre räumlichen Eigenschaften wie Volumen und Oberfläche definiert werden kann."@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050157> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Beispiele sind Formen wie Würfel, Kugeln und Pyramiden."@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050157> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Examples include shapes like cubes, spheres, and pyramids."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060006
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060006> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000033> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060006> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060006> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Hossein Beygi Nasrabadi" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "device specification"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060006> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A directive information entity that outlines the technical requirements, features, constraints, and performance criteria of a specific device, guiding its design, manufacturing, operation, or maintenance."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060006> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060007
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060007> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000033> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "material specification"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060007> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A directive information entity that defines the composition, properties, performance criteria, and acceptable standards for a material, guiding its selection, processing, and application in a specific context."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060007> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060008
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060008> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000104> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "recipe"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060008> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A plan specification that outlines the ingredients, proportions, and procedural steps required to prepare a specific product, typically in cooking, manufacturing, or chemical processes."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060009
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060009> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000033> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060009> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060009> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Hossein Beygi Nasrabadi" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The intent of the specification datum is to express the \"Sollwert\" of some qualitiy or behavioral material property. Then, the specification datum can be further specified by  some value specification."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "specification datum"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060009> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A directive information entity that provides information of a setpoint of some value, i.e., it is an intended value."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060009> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The setpoint value of a ultimate tensile strength of some steel material"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0060009> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080007
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080007> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080007> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080007> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'radiologic quality' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080007> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "radiologic disposition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "radiologische Eigenschaft"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080007> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Radiologic disposition pertains to properties or characteristics related to an entity's interaction with radiant energy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080007> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Radiologische Qualität bezieht sich auf die Eigenschaften oder Merkmale im Zusammenhang mit der Wechselwirkung einer Entität mit Strahlungsenergie"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080007> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The dose equivalent a patient receives from a chest X-ray is a radiologic quality of the examination"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080007> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080010
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080010> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000145> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080010> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080010> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'spatial relational quality' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'BFO_0000145'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080010> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "räumliche Relationsqualität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "spatial relational quality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080010> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Räumliche Beziehungsqualität ist eine Qualität, die einer materiellen Entität aufgrund ihrer räumlichen Beziehung zu einer oder mehreren anderen Entitäten, wie z. B. Position, Ausrichtung oder Entfernung, innewohnt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080010> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Spatial relational quality is a quality that inheres in a material entity by virtue of its spatial relationship to one or more other entities, such as position, orientation, or distance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080010> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "the distance between a bolt and the nearest edge of a steel plate is a spatial relational quality of the bolt"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080010> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'speed' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical process characteristic'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speed."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speed> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Geschwindigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "speed"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Geschwindigkeit beschreibt die Entfernung, die ein Objekt in einer bestimmten Zeit zurücklegt, immer positiv"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "process attribute that describes the distance an object moves in a given amount of time, always positive"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If a train takes 1 hour to travel 100 kilometers, it has a speed of 100 kilometers per hour (62 mph)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080012
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080012> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080012> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080012> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080012> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'electric current' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical process characteristic'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080012> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080012> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "electric current"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080012> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "elektrischer Strom"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080012> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "electric current"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080012> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Elektrischer Strom ist der Fluss elektrischer Ladung pro Zeiteinheit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080012> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "process attribute that represents the flow of electric charge per unit time"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080012> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A 100 W incandescent bulb draws an electric current of about 0.43 A at 230 V"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080012> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'force rate' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical process characteristic'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Kraftrate"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "force rate"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Ruck"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "yank"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "In der Physik wird der Begriff \"Ruck\" manchmal verwendet, um die Ableitung der Kraft in Bezug auf die Zeit oder die mit dem Ruck multiplizierte Masse zu bezeichnen. In der relativistischen Physik wird dieser Begriff als die zweite Ableitung des Impulses in Bezug auf die Zeit ausgedrückt, da die Masse geschwindigkeitsabhängig ist. Obwohl nicht allgemein als offizieller Begriff für diese Größe anerkannt, wird der Begriff \"Ruck\" häufig von Physikbegeisterten verwendet"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "In physics, yank is sometimes used to denote the derivative of force with respect to time or mass multiplied by jerk. In relativistic physics, it is expressed as the second derivative of momentum with respect to time, because the mass is velocity-dependent. Though not universally accepted as an official term for this quantity, the term \"yank\" is commonly used among physics enthusiasts"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "During impact testing, the force rate on the specimen rises to 10 kN/ms within the first microsecond"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080013> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080014
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080014> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080014> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080014> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080014> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'mass flow rate' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical process characteristic'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_flow_rate."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080014> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080014> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_flow_rate> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080014> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Massendurchsatz"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080014> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mass flow rate"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080014> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Der Massendurchfluss quantifiziert die pro Zeiteinheit fließende Masse und wird üblicherweise in Kilogramm pro Sekunde oder Pfund pro Sekunde gemessen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080014> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "process attribute that quantifies the mass passing per unit time, commonly measured in kilograms per second or pounds per second"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080014> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A coolant pump delivers a mass flow rate of 2 kg/s of water through a heat exchanger"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080014> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080015
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080015> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080015> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080015> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080015> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'mechanical impulse' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical process characteristic'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impulse_(physics)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080015> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080015> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impulse_(physics)> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080015> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mechanical impulse"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080015> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mechanischer Impuls"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080015> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Unter mechanischem Impuls versteht man die Änderung des Impulses eines Objekts, wenn es im Laufe der Zeit einer Kraft ausgesetzt wird"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080015> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "process attribute that signifies the change in momentum of an object when subjected to a force over time"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080015> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A drop weight imparts a mechanical impulse of 50 N·s to the Charpy specimen during impact"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080015> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080016
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080016> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080016> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080016> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'radiant energy flux' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical process characteristic'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radiant_energy."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080016> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080016> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radiant_energy> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Strahlungsfluss"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "radiant energy flux"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080016> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Strahlungsfluss beschreibt die Strahlungsenergie, die pro Zeiteinheit emittiert, reflektiert, übertragen oder empfangen wird"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080016> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "process attribute that represents the radiant energy emitted, reflected, transmitted, or received per unit time"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080016> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A solar panel receives a radiant energy flux of 1000 W/m2 under standard test conditions"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080016> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080017
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080017> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080017> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080017> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080017> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'temperature profile' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical process characteristic'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080017> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080017> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Temperaturprofil"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080017> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "temperature profile"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080017> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Temperatur Profil beschreibt Änderungen der Temperatur eines materiellen Wesens oder Raums über die Zeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080017> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "process attribute that describes changes in the temperature of a material entity or space over time"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080017> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The temperature profile along a quenched steel bar varies from 850 C at the surface to 200 C at the core"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080017> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080019
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080019> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080019> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020132> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080019> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080019> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'area' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'DimensionQuality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001323."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080019> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080019> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001323> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080019> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fläche"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080019> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "area"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080019> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Area signifies a 2-D extent quality inhering by virtue of the bearer's two-dimensional extent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080019> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Fläche bedeutet eine zweidimensionale Ausdehnungsqualität, die aufgrund der zweidimensionalen Ausdehnung des Trägers inhärent ist"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080019> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The cross-sectional area of a tensile specimen at the gauge section is 50 mm2"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080019> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
