<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080024> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080024> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'dielectric strength' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'electrical quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080024> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080024> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Durchschlagsfestigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080024> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dielectric strength"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080024> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Dielektrische Festigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080024> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "E_ds"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080024> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Dielectric strength is an electrical quality of an insulating material that specifies the maximum electric field intensity the material can sustain without undergoing electrical breakdown"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080024> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Durchschlagsfestigkeit ist eine elektrische Qualität eines Isoliermaterials, die die maximale elektrische Feldstärke angibt, die das Material aushalten kann, ohne einen elektrischen Durchschlag zu erleiden"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080024> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'magnetic flux' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'magnetic quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "magnetic flux"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "magnetischer Fluss"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Magnetfeld"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "magnetic field"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "magnetic flux"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "magnetischer Fluss"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Magnetischer Fluss ist die Gesamtanzahl der Magnetfeldlinien, die durch eine bestimmte Fläche verlaufen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "magnetic quality that represents the total number of magnetic field lines passing through a given area"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A transformer core carries a magnetic flux of 1 mWb through its cross-section at rated voltage"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080025> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'magnetic permeability' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'magnetic quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "magnetic permeability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "magnetische Permeabilität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Permeabilität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "permeability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "μ"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Magnetic permeability is a magnetic quality of a material that quantifies its ability to support the formation of a magnetic field within itself, expressed as the ratio of magnetic flux density to the applied magnetic field intensity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Magnetische Permeabilität ist eine magnetische Qualität eines Materials, die seine Fähigkeit quantifiziert, ein Magnetfeld in seinem Inneren zu unterstützen, ausgedrückt als Verhältnis der magnetischen Flussdichte zur aufgebrachten magnetischen Feldstärke"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080026> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'coercivity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'magnetic quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Koerzitivfeldstärke"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "coercivity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "H_c"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Koerzitivkraft"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "coercive field"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "coercive force"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Coercivity is a magnetic quality of a ferromagnetic material that specifies the magnitude of the applied magnetic field required to reduce its magnetization to zero after it has been fully magnetised"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Koerzitivfeldstärke ist eine magnetische Qualität eines ferromagnetischen Materials, die die Stärke des aufzubringenden Magnetfelds angibt, das erforderlich ist, um seine Magnetisierung nach vollständiger Magnetisierung auf null zu reduzieren"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080027> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
