<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080029> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080029> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dehnung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080029> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "strain"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080029> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Strain is defined as relative deformation, compared to a reference position configuration"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080029> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Under a tensile load, a polymer film exhibits a strain of 2 % before yielding"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080029> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080029> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'engineering strain' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'strain'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strain_(mechanics)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strain_(mechanics)> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "engineering strain"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "technische Dehnung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Cauchy strain"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "technical strain"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die technische Dehnung oder Cauchy-Dehnung drückt die Gesamtverformung relativ zur ursprünglichen Abmessung des Materials unter Last aus und spiegelt die Dehnung bei axialer Belastung wider"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Engineering strain, or Cauchy strain, expresses total deformation relative to the initial dimension of the material under load, reflecting elongation in axial loading"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A tensile specimen elongates from 50 mm to 55 mm gauge length, giving an engineering strain of 10 %"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080030> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
