<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080031> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Kriechdehnung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "creep strain"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080031> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Creep strain occurs when a material is subjected to constant stress over a long period of time"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080031> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A nickel alloy turbine blade accumulates 0.5 % creep strain after 10000 hours at 900 C"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080029> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'true strain' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'strain'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strain_(mechanics)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strain_(mechanics)> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "true strain"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "wahre Dehnung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Hencky strain"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "logarithmic strain"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "True strain, or logarithmic strain, integrates incrementally over deformation; related to engineering strain as ε=ln(1+e)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Wahre Dehnung, auch als logarithmische Dehnung bekannt, integriert sich schrittweise über die Verformung; in Beziehung zum technischen Dehnungsmaß als ε=ln(1+e)"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "At a cross-section reduction of 50 %, the true strain is ln(2) = 0.693"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080032> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
