# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020335> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0023004> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid2072 .
_:genid2072 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020339> .
_:genid2072 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054> .
_:genid2072 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid2073 .
_:genid2073 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001> .
_:genid2073 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000052> .
_:genid2073 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "StrainAtBreak(x) ↔ Strain(x) ∧ ∃b∃p∃i(obo:BFO_0000040(b) ∧ MeasurementProcess(p) ∧ MeasurementInformationContentEntity(i) ∧ bearerOf(b, x) ∧ describes(i, x) ∧ isOutputOf(i, p) ∧ ∃t(TimeOfBreak(t) ∧ occupiesTemporalRegion(p, t)))"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bruchdehnung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "strain at break"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "elongation at break"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bruchdehnung ist die Dehnung einer Probe im Moment des Bruchs, bestimmt unter Zugbelastung gemäß anwendbaren Prüfnormen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Strain at break is the strain of a specimen at the moment of fracture, determined under tensile load according to applicable test standards"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Strain at break of a thermoplastic polyurethane specimen measured as 450% under ISO 527 test conditions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080033> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080029> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'elastic strain' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'strain'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plasticity_(physics)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plasticity_(physics)> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "elastic strain"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "elastische Deformation"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "elastic deformation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "elastische Verformung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bei der elastischen Dehnung handelt es sich um eine Dehnungsqualität eines Materialgebildes, die durch eine reversible Verformung gekennzeichnet ist, die bei Wegnahme der aufgebrachten Last verschwindet"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Elastic strain is a strain quality of a material entity characterized by reversible deformation that disappears upon removal of the applied load"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Steel loaded to 200 MPa exhibits an elastic strain of about 0.001, fully recovered upon unloading"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080029> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'plastic strain' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'strain'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plasticity_(physics)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plasticity_(physics)> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "plastic strain"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "plastische Deformation"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "plastic deformation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "plastische Verformung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Plastic strain describes permanent deformation occurring when a material is subjected to stress beyond its elastic limit"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Plastische Deformation beschreibt die dauerhafte Verformung, die auftritt, wenn ein Material einer Belastung ausgesetzt wird, die über seine elastische Grenze hinausgeht"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "After exceeding yield strength, a steel rod undergoes 5 % plastic strain that remains after unloading"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080035> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'luminous intensity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'optical quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Lichtstärke in cd gemessen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "luminous intensity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Leuchtintensität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Lichtintensität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "luminous intensity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Lichtstärke ist die Menge des sichtbaren Lichts, das pro Einheitswinkel in eine bestimmte Richtung von einer Quelle abgestrahlt wird, gemessen in Candela (cd)"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Luminous intensity quantifies the visible light emitted per unit solid angle in a particular direction from a source, measured in candela (cd)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A standard LED lamp emits a luminous intensity of 800 cd in the forward direction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080036> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080037
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080037> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080037> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000143> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080037> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080037> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'exposure' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'optical quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exposure_(photography)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080037> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080037> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exposure_(photography)> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080037> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Belichtungszeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080037> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "light exposure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080037> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Exposure in photography refers to the amount of light per unit area reaching film or sensor, determined by shutter speed, lens F-number, and scene luminance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080037> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Unter Belichtung versteht man in der Fotografie die Lichtmenge pro Flächeneinheit, die den Film oder Sensor erreicht, bestimmt durch Verschlusszeit, Blendenzahl des Objektivs und Helligkeit der Szene"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080037> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'Curie temperature' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermo dynamic quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Curie temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Curie-Temperatur"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Curie point"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Curie-Punkt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "T_C"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Curie temperature is a thermodynamic quality of a ferromagnetic material that specifies the temperature above which it loses its permanent magnetic ordering and becomes paramagnetic"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Curie-Temperatur ist eine thermodynamische Qualität eines ferromagnetischen Materials, die die Temperatur angibt, oberhalb derer das Material seine permanente magnetische Ordnung verliert und paramagnetisch wird"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080038> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080039
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080039> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080039> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020313> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080039> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080039> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'specific heat capacity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermo dynamic quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080039> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080039> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "specific heat capacity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080039> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "spezifische Wärmekapazität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080039> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Specific heat capacity is the heat capacity of a sample divided by its mass, representing the heat required to raise temperature by one unit"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080039> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Spezifische Wärmekapazität ist die Wärmekapazität einer Probe geteilt durch ihre Masse und repräsentiert die erforderliche Wärme, um die Temperatur um eine Einheit zu erhöhen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080039> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Water has a specific heat capacity of 4182 J/(kg·K), making it an effective coolant"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080039> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080040
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080040> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080040> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020164> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080040> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080040> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'eutectic point' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermo dynamic quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080040> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080040> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "eutectic point"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080040> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "eutektischer Punkt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080040> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "eutectic temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080040> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "eutektische Temperatur"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080040> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Eutectic point is a thermodynamic quality of a multi-component material system that specifies the composition and temperature at which all components simultaneously solidify from a liquid mixture at the lowest possible melting temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080040> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Eutektischer Punkt ist eine thermodynamische Qualität eines Mehrkomponentenmaterialsystems, die die Zusammensetzung und Temperatur angibt, bei der alle Komponenten gleichzeitig aus einer flüssigen Mischung bei der niedrigstmöglichen Schmelztemperatur erstarren"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080040> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080041
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080041> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080041> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080041> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080041> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'critical pressure' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermo dynamic quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080041> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080041> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "critical pressure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080041> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "kritischer Druck"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080041> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "p_c"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080041> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Critical pressure is a thermodynamic quality of a pure substance that specifies the minimum pressure required to liquefy the substance at its critical temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080041> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Kritischer Druck ist eine thermodynamische Qualität einer reinen Substanz, die den Mindestdruck angibt, der erforderlich ist, um die Substanz bei ihrer kritischen Temperatur zu verflüssigen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080041> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080042
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080042> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080042> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080042> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080042> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'critical temperature' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermo dynamic quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080042> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080042> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "critical temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080042> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "kritische Temperatur"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080042> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "T_c"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080042> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Critical temperature is a thermodynamic quality of a pure substance that specifies the temperature above which the substance cannot exist as a liquid regardless of applied pressure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080042> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Kritische Temperatur ist eine thermodynamische Qualität einer reinen Substanz, die die Temperatur angibt, oberhalb derer die Substanz unabhängig vom aufgebrachten Druck nicht als Flüssigkeit existieren kann"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080042> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
