<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080044> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "aging temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080044> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Aging temperature refers to variable temperature during an aging process depending on the desired deposition formations"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080044> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Al-Cu alloys are artificially aged at 175 C to precipitate strengthening phases"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080045
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080045> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080045> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080045> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080045> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'environmental temperature' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'temperature'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080045> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080045> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Umgebungstemperatur"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080045> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "environmental temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080045> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Environmental temperature describes the observed temperature surrounding a tangible object, including room temperature and temperatures measured in test chambers"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080045> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Umgebungstemperatur ist die Eigenschaft, die die beobachtete Temperatur in der Umgebung eines betrachteten materiellen Objekts beschreibt. Dazu gehören Raumtemperatur und die in Prüfkammern gemessenen Temperaturen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080045> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A circuit board operates at an environmental temperature of 85 C in a high-reliability application"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080045> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080046
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080046> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080046> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080046> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080046> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'vapor pressure' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermo dynamic quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080046> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080046> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dampfdruck"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080046> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "vapor pressure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080046> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "p*"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080046> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Dampfdruck ist eine thermodynamische Qualität eines Stoffes, die den Druck angibt, den sein Dampf ausübt, wenn er sich bei einer gegebenen Temperatur im thermodynamischen Gleichgewicht mit seiner kondensierten Phase befindet"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080046> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Vapor pressure is a thermodynamic quality of a substance that specifies the pressure exerted by its vapor when in thermodynamic equilibrium with its condensed phase at a given temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080046> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080047
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080047> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080047> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080047> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080047> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'flash point' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermo dynamic quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080047> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080047> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Flammpunkt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080047> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "flash point"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080047> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Flammpunkt ist eine thermodynamische Qualität eines flüchtigen Materials, die die niedrigste Temperatur angibt, bei der sein Dampf an der Materialoberfläche ein zündfähiges Gemisch mit Luft bildet"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080047> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Flash point is a thermodynamic quality of a volatile material that specifies the lowest temperature at which its vapour forms an ignitable mixture with air near the surface of the material"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080047> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'ductile-brittle transition temperature' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermo dynamic quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Duktil-Spröd-Übergangstemperatur"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ductile-brittle transition temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Nullduktilitäts-Übergangstemperatur"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "T_DBTT"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "nil ductility transition temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ductile-brittle transition temperature is a thermodynamic quality of a material that specifies the temperature below which the material exhibits brittle fracture behaviour rather than ductile deformation under impact loading"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Duktil-Spröd-Übergangstemperatur ist eine thermodynamische Qualität eines Materials, die die Temperatur angibt, unterhalb derer das Material unter Schlagbelastung ein sprödes Bruchverhalten anstelle einer duktilen Verformung zeigt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080048> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'glass transition temperature' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'ductile-brittle transition temperature' specific to amorphous and semi-crystalline materials. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glass_transition."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glass_transition> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Glasübergangstemperatur"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "glass transition temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Tg"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Glass transition temperature is a ductile-brittle transition temperature of an amorphous or semi-crystalline material that specifies the temperature at which the material transitions from a hard, glassy state to a soft, rubbery state upon heating"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Glasübergangstemperatur ist eine Duktil-Spröd-Übergangstemperatur eines amorphen oder teilkristallinen Materials, die die Temperatur beschreibt, bei der das Material beim Erwärmen von einem harten, glasartigen in einen weichen, gummiartigen Zustand übergeht"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Glass transition temperature of polycarbonate measured at approximately 147 °C, above which the material softens and loses rigidity, determined according to ISO 11357-2."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080049> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
