<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080052> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080053
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080053> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080053> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080052> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080053> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "melting enthalpy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080053> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "the amount of energy required to convert an entity from solid to liquid aggregtate state at constant temperature and pressure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080053> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080054
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080054> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080054> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080052> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080054> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "enthalpy of vaporization"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080054> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "the amount of energy required to convert an entity from liquid to gaseous aggregtate state at constant temperature and pressure"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'auto-ignition temperature' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermo dynamic quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Selbstzündungstemperatur"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "auto-ignition temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "T_AIT"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Zündtemperatur"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "spontaneous ignition temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Auto-ignition temperature is a thermodynamic quality of a substance that specifies the lowest temperature at which it spontaneously ignites in a normal atmosphere without an external ignition source"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Selbstzündungstemperatur ist eine thermodynamische Qualität eines Stoffes, die die niedrigste Temperatur angibt, bei der er sich in normaler Atmosphäre ohne externe Zündquelle selbst entzündet"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080055> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020316> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Might be a process attribute of a viscous fluid flowing (in a channel)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'Reynolds number' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'FluidDynamicQuality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reynolds_number."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reynolds_number> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reynolds number"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reynolds-Zahl"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Reynolds number is a dimensionless quantity predicting fluid flow patterns, measuring the ratio between inertial and viscous forces"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Reynolds-Zahl ist eine dimensionslose Größe zur Vorhersage von Strömungsmustern in Flüssigkeiten, die das Verhältnis zwischen Trägheits- und Viskosekräften misst"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Flow in a 25 mm pipe at 2 m/s has a Reynolds number of about 50000, indicating turbulent regime"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080056> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080057
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080057> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080057> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080057> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080057> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'odor' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'olfactoric quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000058."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080057> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080057> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000058> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080057> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Geruch"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080057> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "odor"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080057> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Geruch ist eine morphologische Eigenschaft, die einem Träger innewohnt, dessen Moleküle von einem Geruchsrezeptor verteilt und wahrgenommen werden"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080057> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Odor is a morphologic quality inhering in a bearer whose molecules are dispersed and perceived by an odorant receptor"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080057> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The characteristic odor of acetic acid is detectable in dilute vinegar solutions"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080057> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080061
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080061> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080061> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080061> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080061> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'radius' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'length'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0002390."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080061> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080061> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0002390> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080061> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Radius"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080061> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "radius"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080061> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Radius is a length quality equal to the distance from the center of a circle to any endpoint on the circular boundary"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080061> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Radius ist eine Längeneigenschaft, die gleich der Entfernung vom Mittelpunkt eines Kreises zu einem beliebigen Endpunkt auf der Kreisgrenze ist"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080061> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A cylindrical specimen has a radius of 5 mm, giving a cross-sectional area of 78.5 mm2"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080061> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
