# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080066
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080066> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080066> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0040001> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080066> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080066> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'height' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'length'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000119."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080066> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080066> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000119> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080066> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Höhe"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080066> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "height"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080066> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die Höhe ist eine eindimensionale Ausdehnungsqualität, die die vertikale Abmessung eines Objekts oder Raums beschreibt, gemessen von der Basis bis zur Spitze"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080066> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Height is a 1-D extent quality describing the vertical dimension of an object or space, measured from the base to the top"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080066> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A steel column has a height of 3.6 m between floor and ceiling connections"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080066> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
