# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'physical relational quality' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'BFO_0000145'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "physical relational quality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "physisch relative Qualität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die physische Beziehungsqualität bezieht sich auf Eigenschaften oder Merkmale einer Entität, die von ihrer Beziehung zu anderen Entitäten abhängig sind"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Physical relational quality pertains to properties or characteristics of an entity dependent on its relation to other entities"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The coefficient of friction between two surfaces is a physical relational quality inhering in both contacting materials"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080070
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080070> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080070> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080070> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080070> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'physical rate quality' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical relational quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080070> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Rate =(def.) a measure, quantity, or frequency, typically one measured against some other quantity or measure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080070> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080070> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "physical rate quality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080070> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "physische Geschwindigkeitsqualität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080070> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die physikalische Geschwindigkeitsqualität bezeichnet den Quotienten zweier physikalischer Größen in unterschiedlichen Einheiten, der die Änderungsrate einer Größe im Verhältnis zu einer anderen darstellt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080070> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Physical rate quality denotes the quotient of two physical quantities in different units, representing one quantity's rate of change in relation to another"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080070> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The rate of thermal expansion of a metal rod during quenching is a physical rate quality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080070> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080071
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080071> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080071> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080071> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080071> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'emissivity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical rate quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080071> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080071> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Emissionsgrad"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080071> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "emissivity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080071> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Emissivität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080071> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "ε"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080071> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Emissionsgrad ist eine physikalische Ratenqualität einer Materialoberfläche, die das Verhältnis der von der Oberfläche emittierten Wärmestrahlung zu der eines idealen schwarzen Körpers bei gleicher Temperatur ausdrückt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080071> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Emissivity is a physical rate quality of a material surface that expresses the ratio of thermal radiation emitted by the surface to that emitted by a perfect blackbody at the same temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080071> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080072
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080072> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080072> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080072> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080072> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'relative isotopic mass' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical rate quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atomic_mass."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080072> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080072> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atomic_mass> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080072> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "relative Isotopenmasse"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080072> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "relative isotopic mass"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080072> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relative Isotopenmasse bezieht sich auf die Masse eines einzelnen Isotops im Vergleich zu 1/12 der Masse eines Kohlenstoff-12-Atoms"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080072> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relative isotopic mass refers to the mass of a single isotope compared to 1/12 of the mass of a carbon-12 atom"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080072> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The relative isotopic mass of carbon-13 is 13.003 u, slightly heavier than carbon-12"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080072> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080073
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080073> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080073> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080073> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080073> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'luminous efficacy' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical rate quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luminous_efficacy."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080073> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080073> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luminous_efficacy> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080073> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Lichtausbeute"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080073> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "luminous efficacy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080073> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die Lichtausbeute misst, wie gut eine Lichtquelle sichtbares Licht erzeugt, berechnet als Lichtstrom geteilt durch Leistung, ausgedrückt in Lumen pro Watt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080073> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Luminous efficacy measures how well a light source produces visible light, calculated as luminous flux divided by power, expressed in lumens per watt"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080073> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A modern LED achieves a luminous efficacy of 200 lm/W, far exceeding incandescent bulbs"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080073> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080074
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080074> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080074> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080074> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080074> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'optical absorptance' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical rate quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080074> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080074> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "optical absorptance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080074> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "optische Absorption"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080074> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die optische Absorption definiert das Verhältnis der absorbierten Strahlungsleistung zur einfallenden Strahlungsleistung und gibt Aufschluss über die Absorptionsfähigkeit eines Mediums"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080074> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Optical absorptance defines the ratio of absorbed radiant power to incident radiant power, indicating a medium's absorption capability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080074> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A solar absorber coating has an optical absorptance of 0.96, converting most sunlight to heat"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080074> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080075
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080075> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080075> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080075> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080075> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'optical transmittance' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical rate quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080075> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080075> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "optical transmittance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080075> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "optische Transmittance"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080075> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die optische Durchlässigkeit wird durch das Verhältnis der übertragenen Strahlungsleistung zur einfallenden Strahlungsleistung definiert und dient der Beurteilung der Übertragungseffizienz"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080075> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Optical transmittance is defined by the ratio of transmitted radiant power to incident radiant power, assessing transmission efficiency"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080075> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A 3 mm thick soda-lime glass pane has an optical transmittance of 90 % in the visible range"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080075> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'mass diffusivity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical rate quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Massendiffusivität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mass diffusivity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "D"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Diffusionskoeffizient"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "diffusion coefficient"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Mass diffusivity is a physical rate quality of a material that quantifies the rate at which a diffusing substance moves through it per unit concentration gradient, as described by Fick's first law"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Massendiffusivität ist eine physikalische Ratenqualität eines Materials, die die Geschwindigkeit beschreibt, mit der eine diffundierende Substanz pro Konzentrationsgradienten durch das Material transportiert wird, gemäß dem ersten Fickschen Gesetz"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080076> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080077
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080077> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080077> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080077> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080077> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'optical reflectance' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical rate quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080077> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080077> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "optical reflectance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080077> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "optische Reflexion"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080077> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Der optische Reflexionsgrad wird durch das Verhältnis der reflektierten Strahlungsleistung zur einfallenden Strahlungsleistung definiert und bewertet die Reflexionsfähigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080077> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Optical reflectance is defined by the ratio of reflected radiant power to incident radiant power, assessing reflective capacity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080077> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A silver mirror has an optical reflectance of 98 % at 600 nm wavelength"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080077> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'electromotive force' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical rate quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electromotive_force."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electromotive_force> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Quellenspannung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "electromotive force"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "EMP"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Electromotive force refers to energy transferred to an electric circuit per unit charge, measured in volts, produced by transducers converting forms of energy to electrical energy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Unter elektromotorischer Kraft versteht man die Energie, die pro Ladungseinheit auf einen Stromkreis übertragen wird. Sie wird in Volt gemessen und von Wandlern erzeugt, die Energieformen in elektrische Energie umwandeln"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A standard zinc-copper galvanic cell produces an electromotive force of 1.1 V"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080078> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080079
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080079> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080079> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080079> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080079> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'humidity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical rate quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080079> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080079> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Feuchtigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080079> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "humidity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080079> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die Luftfeuchtigkeit charakterisiert den Partialdruck der Luft, der durch den Wasserdampfgehalt entsteht, definiert als das Verhältnis von Wassermasse zu Volumen des Medium-Wasser-Gemisches"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080079> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Humidity characterizes air's partial pressure exerted by water vapor content, defined as the mass of water to volume of the medium-water mixture"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080079> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A drying oven maintains relative humidity below 5 % to prevent moisture absorption in polymer samples"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080079> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080080
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080080> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080080> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080080> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080080> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'thermal diffusivity' have not yet been formalized. Although thermal diffusivity is defined as a ratio of thermal conductivity to the product of density and specific heat capacity, a co-inherence axiom cannot uniquely identify this quality among all rate qualities of the same bearer. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical rate quality'."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080080> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080080> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Temperaturleitfähigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080080> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "thermal diffusivity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080080> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Thermische Diffusivität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080080> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "α"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080080> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Temperaturleitfähigkeit ist eine physikalische Ratenqualität eines Materials, die die Geschwindigkeit beschreibt, mit der Wärmeenergie im Verhältnis zur Wärmespeicherkapazität geleitet wird, ausgedrückt als Verhältnis der Wärmeleitfähigkeit zum Produkt aus Dichte und spezifischer Wärmekapazität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080080> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Thermal diffusivity is a physical rate quality of a material that quantifies the rate at which thermal energy is conducted relative to its capacity to store heat, expressed as the ratio of thermal conductivity to the product of density and specific heat capacity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080080> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'work hardening coefficient' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical rate quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Verfestigungsexponent"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "work hardening coefficient"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Kaltverfestigungsexponent"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "n"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "strain hardening exponent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Verfestigungsexponent ist eine physikalische Ratenqualität eines Materials, die die Geschwindigkeit beschreibt, mit der die Fließspannung bei plastischer Verformung während der Kaltumformung zunimmt, ausgedrückt als Exponent n in der Hollomon-Potenzgesetzbeziehung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Work hardening coefficient is a physical rate quality of a material that quantifies the rate at which flow stress increases with plastic strain during cold working, expressed as the exponent n in the Hollomon power-law relation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080081> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
