<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080088> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080088> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080088> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080088> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'dose equivalent' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical relational quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://www.nrc.gov/reading-rm/basic-ref/glossary/dose-equivalent.html."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080088> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080088> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://www.nrc.gov/reading-rm/basic-ref/glossary/dose-equivalent.html> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080088> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dose equivalent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080088> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Äquivalentdosis"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080088> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Das Dosisäquivalent misst die biologische Schädigung lebenden Gewebes durch Strahlenexposition, berechnet als absorbierte Dosis multipliziert mit einem Qualitätsfaktor und ausgedrückt in Rems oder Sievert"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080088> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Dose equivalent measures biological damage to living tissue from radiation exposure, calculated as absorbed dose multiplied by a quality factor, and expressed in rems or sieverts"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080088> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A radiation worker receives a dose equivalent of 2 mSv per year from occupational exposure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080088> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080089
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080089> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080089> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080089> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080089> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'radiant energy density' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'density'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radiant_energy."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080089> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080089> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radiant_energy> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080089> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Strahlungsenergiedichte"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080089> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "radiant energy density"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080089> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Radiant energy density quantifies radiant energy per unit volume"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080089> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Strahlungsenergiedichte misst die Strahlungsenergie pro Volumeneinheit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080089> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The radiant energy density at the focal spot of a laser is 1 GJ/m3 during material processing"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080089> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080091
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080091> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080091> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080091> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080091> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'pixel density' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'number density'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080091> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080091> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pixeldichte"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080091> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pixel density"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080091> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Pixel density describes the relationship between the number of pixels and the area they occupy on a related entity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080091> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Pixeldichte beschreibt das Verhältnis zwischen der Anzahl der Pixel und der Fläche, die sie auf einer verwandten Entität einnehmen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080091> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A 4K display panel has a pixel density of 210 ppi, providing sharp text rendering"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080091> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080092
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080092> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080092> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080092> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080092> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'electric flux density' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'density'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://www.britannica.com/science/electric-flux."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080092> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080092> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://www.britannica.com/science/electric-flux> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080092> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "electric flux density"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080092> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "elektrische Flussdichte"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080092> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die elektrische Flussdichte misst die Gesamtzahl der elektrischen Kraftlinien, die ein bestimmtes Gebiet schneiden, von positiven Ladungen ausgehen und bei negativen Ladungen enden"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080092> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Electric flux density measures the total number of electric lines of force intersecting a given area, originating on positive charges and terminating on negative charges"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080092> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Near a charged plate, the electric flux density is 8.85e-12 C/m2 per V/m of field strength"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080092> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'birefringence' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical relational quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Doppelbrechung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "birefringence"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Zweistrahl-Brechung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "double refraction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Δn"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Birefringence is a physical relational quality of an optically anisotropic material that specifies the difference in refractive indices along two principal optical axes, causing incident light to split into two rays with different velocities"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Doppelbrechung ist eine physikalische relationale Qualität eines optisch anisotropen Materials, die die Differenz der Brechungsindizes entlang zweier optischer Hauptachsen angibt und bewirkt, dass einfallendes Licht in zwei Strahlen mit unterschiedlichen Geschwindigkeiten aufgespalten wird"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080093> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
