<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080098> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020102> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080098> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080098> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'mass mix ratio' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'mass ratio'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massenverh%C3%A4ltnis."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080098> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080098> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massenverh%C3%A4ltnis> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080098> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Massenmischungsverhältnis"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080098> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mass mix ratio"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080098> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Das Massenmischungsverhältnis stellt das Verhältnis der Massen zweier Mischungskomponenten dar und liefert eine quantitative Beschreibung der Zusammensetzung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080098> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "mass ratio that represents the ratio of masses of two mixture components, providing a quantitative composition description"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080098> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A concrete mix uses a mass mix ratio of cement to aggregate of 1:4 for standard structural applications"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080098> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080099
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080099> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080099> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080099> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080099> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'dry mass' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'mass ratio'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080099> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080099> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Trockenmasse"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080099> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dry mass"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080099> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Trockenmasse bezeichnet die Masse, nachdem einem Objekt die gesamte Feuchtigkeit entzogen wurde, typischerweise durch geeignete Erhitzungsmethoden in einem Ofen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080099> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "mass ratio that represents the mass after removing all humidity from an object, typically using qualified heating methods in an oven"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080099> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A fiber composite sample has a dry mass of 48.5 g after 24 hours in a drying oven at 80 C"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080099> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080100
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080100> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080100> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020102> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080100> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080100> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'mass fraction' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'mass ratio'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massenanteil."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080100> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080100> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massenanteil> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080100> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Massenanteil"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080100> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mass fraction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080100> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Der Massenanteil beschreibt den relativen Anteil einer Masse an der Gesamtmasse einer Mischung, ein gängiges quantitatives Maß"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080100> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "mass ratio that describes the relative proportion of a mass to the total mass of a mixture, a common quantitative measure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080100> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A binary Al-4 wt% Cu alloy has a copper mass fraction of 0.04"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080100> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080101
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080101> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080101> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080069> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080101> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080101> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'mass concentration' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'material composition'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massenkonzentration."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080101> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080101> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massenkonzentration> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080101> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Massenkonzentration"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080101> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mass concentration"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080101> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die Massenkonzentration verknüpft die Masse einer Mischungskomponente mit dem Gesamtvolumen in einer quantitativen Beschreibung, die häufig in Lösungen verwendet wird"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080101> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Mass concentration links mass of a mixture component to the total volume in quantitative description, frequently used in solutions"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080101> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A saline infusion solution has a NaCl mass concentration of 9 g/L"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080101> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080103
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080103> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080103> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020104> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080103> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080103> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'volume concentration' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'volume ratio'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volumenkonzentration."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080103> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080103> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volumenkonzentration> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080103> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Volumenkonzentration"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080103> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "volume concentration"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080103> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Volume concentration links the volume of a mixture component to the total volume, crucial for quantitative composition description"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080103> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Volumenkonzentration verbindet das Volumen eines Mischbestandteils mit dem Gesamtvolumen, entscheidend für die quantitative Zusammensetzungsbeschreibung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080103> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A paint pigment dispersion has a TiO2 volume concentration of 20 %"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080103> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080104
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080104> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080104> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020104> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080104> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080104> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'volume fraction' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'volume ratio'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volumenkonzentration."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080104> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080104> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volumenkonzentration> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080104> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Volumenanteil"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080104> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "volume fraction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080104> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Volume fraction describes the volume of a mixture component relative to the sum of all components' volumes"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080104> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Volumenanteil beschreibt das Volumen eines Mischbestandteils im Verhältnis zur Summe der Volumina aller Bestandteile"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080104> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A dual-phase steel contains a martensite volume fraction of 20 %, controlling its strength-ductility balance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080104> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080105
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080105> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080105> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020104> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080105> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080105> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'volume mix ratio' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'volume ratio'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volumenverh%C3%A4ltnis."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080105> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080105> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volumenverh%C3%A4ltnis> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080105> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mischengehaltverhältnis"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080105> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "volume mix ratio"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080105> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Mischengehaltverhältnis definiert das Verhältnis der Volumina von zwei Mischbestandteilen zueinander"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080105> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Volume mix ratio defines the ratio of volumes of two mixture components to each other"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080105> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An epoxy adhesive is mixed in a volume mix ratio of 2:1 resin to hardener"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080105> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'piezoelectric coefficient' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical relational quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "piezoelectric coefficient"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "piezoelektrischer Koeffizient"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "d"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "piezoelectric constant"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "piezoelektrische Konstante"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Piezoelectric coefficient is a physical relational quality of a material that quantifies the coupling between mechanical stress and electric polarization, expressed as the ratio of electric displacement to applied mechanical stress or the ratio of strain to applied electric field"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Piezoelektrischer Koeffizient ist eine physikalische relationale Qualität eines Materials, die die Kopplung zwischen mechanischer Spannung und elektrischer Polarisation quantifiziert, ausgedrückt als Verhältnis der elektrischen Verschiebung zur angelegten mechanischen Spannung oder des Dehnungsanteils zum angelegten elektrischen Feld"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The d33 piezoelectric coefficient of PZT ceramics is about 400 pC/N, enabling sensitive force sensing"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080106> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080107
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080107> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080107> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080107> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080107> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'clamping pressure' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'pressure'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080107> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080107> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Klemmdruck"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080107> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "clamping pressure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080107> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clamping pressure describes the force per area used during the mounting process of a sample, typically involving grips or similar tools"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080107> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Klemmdruck ist die Eigenschaft, die als quantitativer Wert die Kraft pro Fläche beschreibt, die beim Einbau einer Probe, eines Prüfkörpers oder eines Prüfstücks aufgebracht wird, typischerweise verbunden mit einer Art von Klemm- oder Spannzubehör"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080107> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A hydraulic fixture applies a clamping pressure of 5 MPa to hold a workpiece during machining"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080107> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080108
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080108> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080108> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020311> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080108> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0023004> .
