_:genid2133 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Thermodynamic view on stress"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080109
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080109> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080109> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080108> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080109> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080109> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'engineering stress' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'stress'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080109> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080109> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "engineering stress"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080109> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "technische Spannung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080109> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Engineering stress quantifies the internal force per unit area a material experiences under load, assuming the area remains constant"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080109> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Technische Spannung beschreibt die innere Kraft pro Fläche, die ein Material unter Last erfährt, unter der Annahme, dass die Fläche konstant bleibt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080109> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "At yield, a steel specimen with 50 mm2 cross-section under 12.5 kN shows engineering stress of 250 MPa"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080109> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
_:genid2135 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom> .
_:genid2135 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080109> .
_:genid2135 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> .
_:genid2135 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080108> .
_:genid2135 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Express that force and area are properties of the anchor/independent of \"TQC of the deformation process\""@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080110
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080110> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080110> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080108> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080110> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080110> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'true stress' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'stress'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080110> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080110> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "true stress"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080110> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "wahre Spannung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080110> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "True stress is defined using the cauchy stress tensor, relating stress to the current surface size of a volume element"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080110> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Wahre Spannung wird unter Verwendung des Cauchy-Spannungstensors definiert und bezieht die Spannung auf die aktuelle Oberflächengröße eines Volumenelements"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080110> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "At 10 % engineering strain in a tensile test, the true stress exceeds the engineering stress by the same factor"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080110> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
