_:genid2145 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> _:genid2137 .
_:genid2145 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "strictly speaking this is just stress sustained over time."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080112
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080112> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080112> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080112> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080112> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'adhesion' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'pressure'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080112> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080112> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Adhäsion"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080112> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "adhesion"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080112> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Adhesion describes the ability of substances to bind to each other, involving attractive force between two bodies of different substances in contact and influencing material performance in scientific and industrial contexts"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080112> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Adhäsion beschreibt die Fähigkeit von Substanzen, sich aneinander zu binden. Dabei handelt es sich um eine Anziehungskraft zwischen zwei in Kontakt stehenden Körpern unterschiedlicher Substanzen, die die Materialleistung in wissenschaftlichen und industriellen Kontexten beeinflusst"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080112> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The adhesion between a paint film and a steel substrate determines its resistance to delamination"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080112> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0023045> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'surface tension' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'adhesion'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Oberflächenspannung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "surface tension"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Oberflächenspannung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "surface stress"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "surface tension"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Oberflächenspannung bezeichnet den Effekt innerhalb der Oberflächenschicht einer Flüssigkeit, der durch Wechselwirkungskräfte zwischen ihren Molekülen verursacht wird"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Surface tension refers to the effect within the surface layer of a liquid/gas interface, caused by intermolecular forces between its molecules"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Water has a surface tension of 72.8 mN/m at 20 C, enabling capillary rise in fine tubes"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080113> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid2146 .
_:genid2146 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115> .
_:genid2146 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051> .
_:genid2146 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'refractive index' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical relational quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Refractive_index#Complex_index_of_refraction_and_absorption."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Refractive_index#Complex_index_of_refraction_and_absorption> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Brechzahl"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "refractive index"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Brechzahl gibt die Lichtbrechungsfähigkeit eines optischen Mediums an; umfasst einen realen und einen imaginären Teil, der als Extinktionskoeffizient bekannt ist"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Refractive index indicates an optical medium's light bending ability; encompassing a real and imaginary part known as the extinction coefficient"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Optical glass BK7 has a refractive index of 1.52 at 589 nm, bending light in lenses"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080114> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'extinction coefficient' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'refractive index'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Refractive_index#Complex_index_of_refraction_and_absorption."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Refractive_index#Complex_index_of_refraction_and_absorption> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Extinktionskoeffizient"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "extinction coefficient"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Der Extinktionskoeffizient, die imaginäre Komponente des komplexen Brechungsindex, gibt die Dämpfung elektromagnetischer Wellen durch ein Material an"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Extinction coefficient, the imaginary component of the complex refractive index, indicates attenuation of electromagnetic waves through a material"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The extinction coefficient of gold at 500 nm wavelength is 1.87, characterizing strong optical absorption"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080115> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
