# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020309> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020313> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid2154 .
_:genid2154 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000146> .
_:genid2154 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025999> .
_:genid2154 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'heat transfer coefficient' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical relational quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heat_transfer_coefficient."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heat_transfer_coefficient> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Wärmeübergangskoeffizient"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "heat transfer coefficient"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Der Wärmeübertragungskoeffizient stellt die Proportionalitätskonstante zwischen dem Wärmefluss und der thermodynamischen Antriebskraft für den Wärmefluss dar und wird zur Berechnung der Wärmeübertragung, typischerweise durch Konvektion, verwendet"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Heat transfer coefficient represents the proportionality constant between heat flux and the thermodynamic driving force for heat flow, used in calculating heat transfer, typically by convection"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A forced convection air-cooled heat sink has a heat transfer coefficient of 100 W/(m2·K)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080119> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080120
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080120> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080120> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080120> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080120> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'magnetic susceptibility' have not yet been formalized. Although χ = M/H is a well-defined ratio, a formal equivalence axiom would incorrectly classify any dimensionless relational quality of a magnetic bearer as magnetic susceptibility. Defined as a primitive subtype of 'physical relational quality'."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080120> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080120> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "magnetic susceptibility"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080120> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "magnetische Suszeptibilität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080120> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "χ"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080120> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Magnetic susceptibility is a physical relational quality of a material that quantifies the degree to which it becomes magnetized in response to an applied magnetic field, expressed as the dimensionless ratio of magnetization to applied field intensity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080120> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Magnetische Suszeptibilität ist eine physikalische relationale Qualität eines Materials, die den Grad angibt, in dem es sich als Reaktion auf ein angelegtes Magnetfeld magnetisiert, ausgedrückt als dimensionsloses Verhältnis der Magnetisierung zur angelegten Feldstärke"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080120> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Paramagnetic oxygen gas has a positive magnetic susceptibility of 3.73e-6 m3/mol at 20 C"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080120> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'fluid permeability' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical relational quality'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fluiddurchlässigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "fluid permeability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Darcy permeability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Durchlässigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "hydraulic permeability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "k"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Fluid permeability is a physical relational quality of a porous material that quantifies its capacity to allow fluid flow through its pore network under an applied pressure gradient, defined by Darcy's law as the ratio of fluid flux to the pressure gradient normalized by fluid viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Fluiddurchlässigkeit ist eine physikalische relationale Qualität eines porösen Materials, die seine Fähigkeit quantifiziert, Fluidfluss durch sein Porennetzwerk unter einem angelegten Druckgradienten zu ermöglichen, definiert durch das Darcy-Gesetz als Verhältnis des Fluidflusses zum Druckgradienten normiert durch die Viskosität des Fluids"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Sandstone with a Darcy permeability of 100 mD allows significant fluid flow under pressure gradients"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080121> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080122
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080122> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080122> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080122> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080122> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'phase velocity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'speed'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080122> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080122> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Phasengeschwindigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080122> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "phase velocity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080122> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die Phasengeschwindigkeit bezieht sich auf die Geschwindigkeit, mit der sich die Phase einer Welle ausbreitet, definiert als Wellenlänge geteilt durch die Zeitperiode"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080122> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Phase velocity refers to the rate at which the phase of a wave propagates, defined as wavelength divided by time period"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080122> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The phase velocity of a longitudinal ultrasonic wave in steel is approximately 5900 m/s"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080122> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080011> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'deformation speed' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'speed'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strain_rate."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strain_rate> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Deformationsgeschwindigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "deformation speed"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Dehnrate"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "strain rate"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Deformation speed measures the rate at which distances of adjacent material parcels change with time near a specific point, including expansion and shear rates"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die Verformungsgeschwindigkeit misst die Geschwindigkeit, mit der sich die Abstände benachbarter Materialpakete in der Nähe eines bestimmten Punktes im Laufe der Zeit ändern, einschließlich Expansions- und Schergeschwindigkeiten"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "During high-rate forming, the deformation speed of the punch reaches 10 m/s"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080123> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
