<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080125> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'sound insulation index' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'acoustic capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080125> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080125> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Schalldämmmaß"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080125> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sound insulation index"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080125> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Schalldämmmaß quantifiziert die Fähigkeit eines Materials, die Schallübertragung zu reduzieren"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080125> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Sound insulation index quantifies the ability of a material to reduce sound transmission"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080125> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A 200 mm concrete wall achieves a sound insulation index of 52 dB, blocking most airborne noise"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080125> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
