<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080128> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'electrical resistance' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'electrical capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://www.britannica.com/technology/resistance-electronics."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080128> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080128> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://www.britannica.com/technology/resistance-electronics> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080128> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "electrical resistance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080128> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "elektrischer Widerstand"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080128> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Der elektrische Widerstand bezieht sich auf die Fähigkeit eines Stromkreises, elektrische Energie in Wärmeenergie umzuwandeln, indem er elektrischem Strom durch Teilchenkollisionen entgegenwirkt, die für Widerstände, Lampen und Drähte charakteristisch sind"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080128> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Electrical resistance pertains to a circuit's capability to transform electric energy into heat energy, opposing electric current through particle collisions, characteristic of resistors, lamps, and wires"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080128> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A nichrome heating element has an electrical resistance of 10 Ω at room temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080128> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
