# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080133> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'wear resistance' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'durability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Verschleißfestigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "wear resistance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Verschleißfestigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "resistance to wear"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "wear resistance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "widerstand gegen Verschleiß"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Verschleißfestigkeit ist die Fähigkeit eines Materials, mechanischen Aktionen wie Reiben, Kratzen oder Erosion zu widerstehen, die dazu tendieren, Material allmählich von seiner Oberfläche zu entfernen."@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Wear resistance is the ability of a material to resist mechanical actions such as rubbing, scraping or erosion that tend to progressively remove material from its surface."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Hardened tool steel has high wear resistance, maintaining a cutting edge through thousands of machining cycles"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080134> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080133> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'creep resistance' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'durability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Kriechfestigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "creep resistance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Creep Resistance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Creep Resistant"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Kriechfestig"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Kriechfestigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Creep resistance is the ability of a material to resist deformation under load over time"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die Kriechfestigkeit ist die Fähigkeit eines Materials, unter Last über einen bestimmten Zeitraum eine Deformation zu widerstehen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Nickel superalloys have high creep resistance, maintaining shape under stress at 1000 C in turbine blades"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080135> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'poisson effect' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'mechanical capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poisson%27s_ratio."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Was a subclass of 'Mechanical Quality'" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poisson%27s_ratio> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Querkontraktion"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "poisson effect"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Poisson effect describes deformation perpendicular to the direction of loading, named after Siméon Poisson"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Querkontraktion beschreibt die Deformation senkrecht zur Belastungsrichtung, benannt nach Siméon Poisson"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A rubber cylinder loaded axially expands radially due to the Poisson effect, with a ratio of about 0.5"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080136> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
