# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'aterial fatigue' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'mechanical capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Materialermüdung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "material fatigue"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Ermüdung des Materials"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Materialermüdung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "fatigue of material"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "material fatigue"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Material fatigue is the failure of a material caused by repeated or sustained loading below its ultimate strength."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Materialermüdung ist das Versagen von Werkstoffen infolge wiederholter oder dauernder Belastung unterhalb der Probenfestigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Repeated cyclic loading at 400 MPa induces material fatigue in a steel shaft, leading to crack initiation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080138> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'impact energy' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'mechanical capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Schlagenergie"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "impact energy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Charpy impact energy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "KV"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Kerbschlagenergie"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Impact energy is a mechanical capability of a material that characterises the total energy absorbed by a standardised notched specimen during fracture under a single impact blow, as measured in a Charpy or Izod test"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Schlagenergie ist eine mechanische Fähigkeit eines Materials, die die gesamte Energie beschreibt, die eine standardisierte gekerbte Probe beim Bruch unter einem einzigen Schlagimpuls absorbiert, gemessen im Charpy- oder Izod-Versuch"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080139> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'viscoelasticity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'strength'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Viscoelastizität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "viscoelasticity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Viscoelastizität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Viskoelastizität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "elasticity of viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "viscoelasticity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Viscoelasticity describes materials exhibiting both viscous and elastic characteristics during deformation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Viscoelastizität beschreibt Materialien, die sowohl viskose als auch elastische Eigenschaften während der Verformung zeigen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Polymers exhibit viscoelasticity, showing both elastic recovery and creep under constant load"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080143> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'creep modulus' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'viscoelasticity'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Kriechmodul"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "creep modulus"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Kriechmodul"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "creep modulus"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Creep modulus measures a material's viscoelasticity, indicating its ability to deform under stress over time"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Der Kriechmodul ist ein Maß für die Viskoelastizität eines Materials, das seine Fähigkeit zur Verformung unter Belastung im Laufe der Zeit beschreibt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The creep modulus of polyethylene at 50 C and 1 MPa after 1000 hours is 200 MPa"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080144> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'complex modulus' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'viscoelasticity'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Komplexmodul"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "complex modulus"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "E*"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Complex modulus is a viscoelastic quality of a material that represents the total stiffness response under oscillatory loading as a complex number, comprising the storage modulus as the real part and the loss modulus as the imaginary part"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Komplexmodul ist eine viskoelastische Qualität eines Materials, die die gesamte Steifigkeitsantwort unter schwingender Belastung als komplexe Zahl darstellt, bestehend aus dem Speichermodul als Realteil und dem Verlustmodul als Imaginärteil"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'loss modulus' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'complex modulus'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamic_modulus."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamic_modulus> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Verlustmodul"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "loss modulus"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "E''"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Loss modulus is the imaginary part of the complex modulus that measures the viscous portion of energy dissipated as heat per cycle in a viscoelastic material under oscillatory loading"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Verlustmodul ist der Imaginärteil des Komplexmoduls und misst den viskosen Anteil der pro Zyklus als Wärme dissipierten Energie in einem viskoelastischen Material unter schwingender Belastung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The loss modulus of a viscoelastic polymer at 1 Hz is 0.3 MPa, representing energy dissipation per cycle"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080146> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'dynamic modulus' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'complex modulus'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamic_modulus."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamic_modulus> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dynamic modulus"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dynamischer Modul"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "complex shear modulus"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Dynamic modulus is the ratio of stress to strain under vibratory conditions, typically measured in shear, compression, or elongation tests, and characterizes viscoelastic materials"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Dynamischer Modul ist das Verhältnis von Spannung zu Dehnung unter schwingenden Bedingungen, typischerweise gemessen in Scher-, Druck- oder Dehnungstests, und charakterisiert viskoelastische Materialien"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The dynamic modulus of a rubber compound at 10 Hz is 15 MPa, relevant for vibration isolation design"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080148
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080148> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080148> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080147> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080148> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080148> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'loss tangent' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'dynamic modulus'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamic_modulus."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080148> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080148> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamic_modulus> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080148> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Verlustwinkel"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080148> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "loss tangent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080148> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Der Verlustfaktor, dargestellt als tan δ, ist das Verhältnis des Verlustmoduls zum Speichermodul in viskoelastischen Materialien und liefert ein Maß für die Dämpfung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080148> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Loss tangent, represented as tan δ, is the ratio of the loss modulus to storage modulus in viscoelastic materials, providing a measure of damping"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080148> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A PTFE cable insulator has a loss tangent of 0.0002 at 1 GHz, minimizing signal attenuation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080148> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080145> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'storage modulus' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'complex modulus'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamic_modulus."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamic_modulus> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Speichermodul"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "storage modulus"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "E'"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Speichermodul ist der Realteil des Komplexmoduls und misst den elastischen Anteil der gespeicherten und zurückgewonnenen Energie pro Zyklus in einem viskoelastischen Material unter schwingender Belastung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Storage modulus is the real part of the complex modulus that measures the elastic portion of energy stored and recovered per cycle in a viscoelastic material under oscillatory loading"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The storage modulus of a polyurethane foam at 1 Hz and 25 C is 0.5 MPa, reflecting its elastic stiffness"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080149> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020335> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'toughness' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'strength'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Zähigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "toughness"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Zähigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "toughness"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Toughness describes the resistance of a material to fracture or crack propagation, determined by its ability to absorb mechanical energy during deformation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Zähigkeit beschreibt die Widerstandsfähigkeit eines Werkstoffs gegen Bruch oder Rissausbreitung, bestimmt durch die Fähigkeit zur Absorption von mechanischer Energie bei Verformung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "High-toughness tool steel absorbs 80 J before fracture in a Charpy V-notch test at room temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'fracture toughness' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'toughness'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bruchzähigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "fracture toughness"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "K_Ic"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "critical stress intensity factor"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bruchzähigkeit ist eine Zähigkeitsqualität eines Materials, die die kritische Spannungsintensität beschreibt, bei der ein vorhandener Riss zu wachsen beginnt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Fracture toughness is a toughness quality of a material that specifies the critical stress intensity at which a pre-existing crack begins to propagate, expressed as the stress intensity factor at the onset of fracture"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Fracture toughness of a high-strength steel measured as 50 MPa·√m according to ISO 17281 test conditions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080151> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080150> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'impact strength' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'toughness'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Schlagzähigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "impact strength"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Schlagfestigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Schlagzähigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "impact strength"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "mpact strength"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Impact strength is the ability of a material to absorb energy and plastically deform without fracturing under dynamic load"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Schlagzähigkeit bezeichnet die Fähigkeit eines Materials, Energie zu absorbieren und bei Anwendung einer dynamischen Last plastisch zu verformen, ohne dass es bricht"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A Charpy impact test on notched steel gives an impact strength of 120 J, indicating good toughness"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080152> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
