<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080171> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The amount of plastic strain typically gives more information about the yield stress. E.g. Rp02 has 0.2% plastic strain."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080171> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fließgrenze"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080171> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "yield stress"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080171> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "yield strength"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080171> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "is the stress at which the material has a non-zero plastic strain."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080171> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The yield strength of mild steel is approximately 250 MPa, beyond which permanent deformation begins"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080171> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
