# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080171> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'lower yield strength' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'yield strength'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yield_(engineering)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yield_(engineering)> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "lower yield strength"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "untere Streckgrenze"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "lower yield stress"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "untere Fließspannung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Lower yield strength defines the stress at which a material exhibits plastic behavior after initial yielding"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Untere Streckgrenze beschreibt die Spannung, bei der ein Material nach dem anfänglichen Fließen plastisches Verhalten zeigt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The lower yield strength of mild steel is approximately 235 MPa, defining the onset of stable plastic flow"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080172> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080171> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'upper yield strength' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'yield strength'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yield_(engineering)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yield_(engineering)> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "obere Streckgrenze"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "upper yield strength"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "obere Fließspannung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "upper yield stress"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Obere Streckgrenze charakterisiert die maximale Spannung, die vor dem plastischen Fließen eines Materials angewendet werden kann"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Upper yield strength characterizes the maximum stress that can be applied before a material begins to yield plastically"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Mild steel exhibits an upper yield strength of about 300 MPa, followed by a yield drop to the lower yield point"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080173> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020316> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'viscosity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'plasticity'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Viskosität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Viskosität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Viscosity measures a fluid's resistance to flow"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Viskosität misst den Widerstand eines Fluids gegen den Fluss"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Honey at 25 C has a viscosity of about 10 Pa·s, flowing slowly under gravity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080175
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080175> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080175> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080175> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080175> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'extentional viscosity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'viscosity'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080175> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080175> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dehnviskosität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080175> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "extentional viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080175> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die Dehnviskosität ist die Messung des Widerstands einer Flüssigkeit gegen den Fluss bei Dehnspannung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080175> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Extentional viscosity measures a fluid's resistance to tension flow"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080175> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A polymer melt shows an extensional viscosity three times its shear viscosity at low strain rates"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080175> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'shear viscosity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'viscosity'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Scherviskosität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "shear viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Scherviskosität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "shear viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Scherviskosität misst den Widerstand eines Fluids gegen Scherfluss"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Shear viscosity measures a fluid's resistance to shear flow"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The shear viscosity of glycerol at 25 C is about 1.5 Pa·s, much higher than water"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080176> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'kinematic viscosity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'viscosity'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "kinematic viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "kinematische Viskosität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "kinematic viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "kinematische Viskosität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "kinetic viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "kinetische Viskosität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die kinematische Viskosität ist das Verhältnis der dynamischen Viskosität zur Dichte"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Kinematic viscosity is the ratio of dynamic viscosity to density"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The kinematic viscosity of water at 20 C is about 1e-6 m2/s, used in pipe flow calculations"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080177> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'dynamic viscosity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'viscosity'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dynamic viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dynamische Viskosität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "dynamic viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "dynamische Viskosität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die dynamische Viskosität ist ein Maß für den Widerstand eines Fluids gegen eine allmähliche Verformung durch Scher- oder Zugspannung. Es ist ein Maß für den inneren Widerstand des Fluids gegen den Fluss und kann als Maß für die Flüssigkeitsreibung betrachtet werden"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Dynamic viscosity measures a fluid's resistance to gradual deformation by shear stress or tensile stress, indicative of the fluid's internal friction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Motor oil at 40 C has a dynamic viscosity of about 100 mPa·s, resisting flow under shear"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080178> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080179
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080179> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080179> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080174> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080179> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080179> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'volume viscosity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'viscosity'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080179> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080179> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Volumenviskosität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080179> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "volume viscosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080179> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Volume viscosity measures a fluid's resistance to volumetric stress"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080179> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Volumenviskosität misst den Widerstand eines Fluids gegenüber volumetrischer Belastung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080179> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Water has a volume viscosity of about 3 mPa·s at 25 C, relevant in acoustic wave propagation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080179> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'brittleness' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'mechanical capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sprödigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "brittleness"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Sprödigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Zerbrechlichkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "brittleness"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "fragility"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Opposite to toughness, brittleness is the property of being easily broken or damaged"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Sprödigkeit ist die Eigenschaft, leicht zu brechen oder zu beschädigen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Cast iron has high brittleness, fracturing without measurable plastic deformation under tensile loading"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080180> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'ductility' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'mechanical capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Duktilität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ductility"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Biegsamkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Duktilität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "ductility"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "flexibility"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ductility is the ability of a material to deform plastically without breaking"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Duktilität ist die Fähigkeit eines Materials, plastisch zu verformen, ohne zu brechen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Low-carbon steel has high ductility, with elongation at break exceeding 30 %"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080181> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'malleability' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'ductility'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Formbarkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "malleability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Formbarkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Malleability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Malleable"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "formbar"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Formbarkeit beschreibt Materialien, die durch Hammern oder Walzen bearbeitet werden können und sich von Duktilität unterscheiden"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Malleability refers to a material's amenability to forming by hammering or rolling, distinct from ductility"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Gold has high malleability, allowing it to be hammered into sheets less than 100 nm thick"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080182> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080184
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080184> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080184> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080184> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080184> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'resilience' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'mechanical capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080184> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080184> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Resilienz"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080184> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "resilience"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080184> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Resilienzmodul"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080184> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "modulus of resilience"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080184> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Elastizität ist die mechanische Fähigkeit eines Materials, bei elastischer Verformung Energie zu absorbieren und diese Energie bei Entlastung ohne bleibende Verformung abzugeben"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080184> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Resilience is a mechanical capability of a material to absorb energy when elastically deformed and release that energy upon unloading without permanent deformation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080184> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080186
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080186> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080186> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080186> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080186> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'radiation reflection capability' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'optical capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080186> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080186> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Strahlungsreflexionsfähigkeiten"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080186> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "radiation reflection capability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Radiation reflection capability characterizes an entity's ability to reflect electromagnetic radiation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Strahlungsreflexionsfähigkeit beschreibt die Fähigkeit einer Entität, elektromagnetische Strahlung zu reflektieren"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Polished aluminum foil has high radiation reflection capability, reflecting 90 % of infrared radiation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080186> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080187
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080187> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080187> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080187> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080187> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'radiation absorption capability' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'optical capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080187> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080187> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Strahlungsabsorptionsfähigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080187> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "radiation absorption capability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080187> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Radiation absorption capability characterizes an entity's ability to absorb electromagnetic radiation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080187> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Strahlungsabsorptionsfähigkeit beschreibt die Fähigkeit einer Entität, elektromagnetische Strahlung zu absorbieren"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080187> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Carbon black pigment has high radiation absorption capability, absorbing over 99 % of incident visible light"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080187> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080188
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080188> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080188> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080188> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080188> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'radiation emission capability' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'optical capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080188> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080188> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Strahlungsemitter"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080188> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "radiation emitter"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080188> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Radiation emission capability refers to an entity's ability to emit light of a defined spectrum and intensity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080188> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Strahlungsemitter beschreibt die Fähigkeit einer Entität, Licht eines definierten Spektrums und Intensität zu emittieren"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080188> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A cobalt-60 source is a radiation emitter used in industrial gamma-ray testing of welds"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080188> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080189
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080189> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080189> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080189> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080189> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'radiation transmission capability' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'optical capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080189> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080189> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Strahlungsübertragungsfähigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080189> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "radiation transmission capability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080189> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Radiation transmission capability describes an entity's ability to transmit electromagnetic radiation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080189> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Strahlungsübertragungsfähigkeit beschreibt die Fähigkeit einer Entität, elektromagnetische Strahlung zu übertragen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080189> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A thin beryllium window has high radiation transmission capability for soft X-rays, passing over 90 % of flux"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080189> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'thermal capacity' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermal capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heat_capacity."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heat_capacity> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "thermal capacity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "thermische Kapazität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Wärmekapazität"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "heat capacity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Thermal capacity, or heat capacity, is defined as the amount of heat required to produce a unit change in temperature of an object"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Wärmekapazität, auch als thermische Kapazität bekannt, ist die Menge an Wärme, die erforderlich ist, um eine Änderung der Temperatur eines Objekts um eine Einheit zu erzeugen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A steel block of 1 kg has a thermal capacity of 500 J/K, absorbing heat with moderate temperature rise"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080191> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080192
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080192> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080192> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080192> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080192> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'flammability' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermal capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080192> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080192> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Entflammbarkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080192> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "flammability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080192> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Brennbarkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080192> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "combustibility"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080192> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Entflammbarkeit ist eine thermische Fähigkeit eines Materials, die seine Fähigkeit beschreibt, bei Exposition gegenüber einer Flamme oder Wärmequelle unter festgelegten Bedingungen zu entzünden und die Verbrennung aufrechtzuerhalten"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080192> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Flammability is a thermal capability of a material that characterises its ability to ignite and sustain combustion when exposed to a flame or heat source under specified conditions"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080192> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080194
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080194> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080194> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080194> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080194> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'thermal insulation' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermal capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermal_insulation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080194> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080194> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermal_insulation> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080194> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "thermal insulation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080194> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "thermische Isolierung"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080194> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Thermal insulation reduces heat transfer between objects in thermal contact or radiative influence, achieved with engineered methods or material properties"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080194> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Thermische Isolierung verringert den Wärmeaustausch zwischen Objekten, die in thermischem Kontakt oder Strahlungseinfluss stehen, realisiert durch spezielle Konstruktionsmethoden oder Materialien"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080194> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Glass wool with a thermal conductivity of 0.04 W/(m·K) provides effective thermal insulation in building walls"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080194> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080195
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080195> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080195> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020142> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080195> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080195> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'radiant energy' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermal capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions. The definition is adapted from: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radiant_energy."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080195> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080195> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radiant_energy> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080195> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Strahlungsenergie"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080195> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "radiant energy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080195> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Radiant energy refers to the energy of electromagnetic radiation, calculated by integrating radiant flux over time"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080195> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Strahlungsenergie bezieht sich auf die Energie elektromagnetischer Strahlung, die durch Integration des Strahlungsflusses über die Zeit berechnet wird"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080195> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A pulsed laser delivers 1 mJ of radiant energy per pulse to the workpiece surface"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080195> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'thermal expansion coefficient' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermal capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "thermal expansion coefficient"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "thermischer Ausdehnungkoeffizient"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Thermal expansion coefficient quantifies the degree to which a material expands upon heating, representing fractional change per degree temperature increase"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Thermischer Ausdehnungkoeffizient quantifiziert den Grad, in dem ein Material beim Erhitzen expandiert, und stellt die proportionale Änderung pro Temperaturanstieg dar"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The thermal expansion coefficient of borosilicate glass is 3.3e-6 per K, enabling thermal shock resistance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080197
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080197> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080197> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080197> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080197> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'volumetric thermal expansion coefficient' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermal expansion coefficient'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080197> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080197> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "thermischer Volumenausdehnungskoeffizient"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080197> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "volumetric thermal expansion coefficient"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080197> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Der volumetrische Wärmeausdehnungskoeffizient quantifiziert den Grad, um den sich ein Material beim gleichzeitigen Erhitzen in alle drei axialen Richtungen ausdehnt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080197> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Volumetric thermal expansion coefficient quantifies the degree to which a material expands upon heating into all three axial directions simultaneously"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080197> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Liquid water near 4 C has a near-zero volumetric thermal expansion coefficient, giving maximum density"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080197> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080198
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080198> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080198> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080196> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080198> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080198> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'linear thermal expansion coefficient' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermal expansion coefficient'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080198> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080198> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "linear thermal expansion coefficient"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080198> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "linearer thermischer Ausdehnungkoeffizient"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080198> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Der lineare Wärmeausdehnungskoeffizient quantifiziert den Grad, um den sich ein Material beim Erhitzen in eine bestimmte axiale Richtung ausdehnt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080198> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Linear thermal expansion coefficient quantifies the degree to which a material expands upon heating into a specific axial direction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080198> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Aluminum has a linear thermal expansion coefficient of 23.1e-6 per K, causing notable dimensional changes during heating"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080198> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080200
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080200> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080200> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080200> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080200> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'flame resistance' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermal capability', disjoint from 'flammability' as the inverse capability. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080200> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080200> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Flammbeständigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080200> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "flame resistance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080200> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Brandbeständigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080200> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "fire resistance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080200> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Flame resistance is a thermal capability of a material that characterises its ability to resist ignition and inhibit the spread of combustion when exposed to a flame or heat source"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080200> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Flammbeständigkeit ist eine thermische Fähigkeit eines Materials, die seine Fähigkeit beschreibt, einer Entzündung zu widerstehen und die Ausbreitung der Verbrennung bei Exposition gegenüber einer Flamme oder Wärmequelle zu verhindern"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080200> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080201
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080201> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080201> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080201> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080201> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'thermal conductance' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermal capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080201> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080201> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "thermal conductance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080201> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "thermische Leitfähigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080201> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Thermal conduction refers to the process by which heat is transferred from the hotter end to the colder end of an object, characterized by conductance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080201> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Thermische Leitung beschreibt den Prozess, bei dem Wärme vom heißeren zum kälteren Ende eines Objekts übertragen wird, gekennzeichnet durch Leitfähigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080201> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A copper heat spreader of 2 mm thickness has a high thermal conductance, efficiently dissipating chip heat"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080201> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080202
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080202> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080202> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080202> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080202> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'thermal shock resistance' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'thermal capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080202> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080202> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Thermoschockbeständigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080202> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "thermal shock resistance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080202> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Temperaturwechselbeständigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080202> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Thermal shock resistance is a thermal capability of a material that characterises its ability to withstand rapid and large changes in temperature without cracking, spalling, or loss of mechanical integrity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080202> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Thermoschockbeständigkeit ist eine thermische Fähigkeit eines Materials, die seine Fähigkeit beschreibt, schnelle und große Temperaturänderungen ohne Rissbildung, Abplatzungen oder Verlust der mechanischen Integrität zu überstehen"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080202> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080203
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080203> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080203> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080007> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080203> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080203> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'radiation emission capability' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080203> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080203> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Strahlungsemissionsfähigkeit"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080203> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "radiation emission capability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080203> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die Strahlungsemissionsfähigkeit ist die physikalische Fähigkeit eines materiellen Wesens, elektromagnetische Strahlung auszusenden, die in Prozessen realisiert wird, bei denen der Träger Energie in Form elektromagnetischer Wellen ausstrahlt"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080203> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Radiation emission capability is a physical capability of a material entity to emit electromagnetic radiation, realized in processes where the bearer radiates energy in the form of electromagnetic waves"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080203> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A tungsten filament at 2800 K has significant radiation emission capability, producing visible white light"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080203> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080204
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080204> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080204> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080204> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080204> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Necessary and sufficient conditions for 'water absorption' have not yet been formalized. The term is defined as a specific subtype of 'physical capability'. Distinguishing criteria are domain-specific and depend on measurement conventions or source terminology not yet expressed as OWL restrictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080204> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Thomas Hanke" .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080204> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Wasseraufnahme"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080204> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "water absorption"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080204> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Wasseraufnahme ist eine physische Fähigkeit eines Materials, Wasser aufzunehmen, quantifiziert als Massenzunahme einer Probe im Verhältnis zur anfänglichen Trockenmasse"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080204> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Water absorption is a physical capability of a material to take up water, quantified as the increase in mass of a specimen relative to its initial dry mass"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080204> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Water absorption of a nylon 6 specimen immersed for 24 hours expressed as 2.5% of its dry mass, measured according to ISO 62."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080204> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
# 
